{"term":"disguise","senses":[{"id":"kaikki:a4062d249d40d5ee7f","definition":"Material (such as clothing, makeup, a wig) used to alter one’s visual appearance in order to hide one's identity or assume another.","example":"A cape and moustache completed his disguise.","pos":"noun","synonyms":["camouflage","mask","guise","pretense","garb"],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"","register":"countable, uncountable","wordFamily":["disguiseless","undisguise"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/disguise#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:5477c5cb2e886eafcd","definition":"The appearance of something on the outside which masks what’s beneath.","example":"old ideas in a new guise","pos":"noun","synonyms":["camouflage","mask","guise","pretense","garb"],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"figuratively","register":"countable, figuratively, uncountable","wordFamily":["disguiseless","undisguise"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/disguise#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:c91dcd2a82b3cd2006","definition":"The act or state of disguising, notably as a ploy.","example":"Any disguise may expose soldiers to be deemed enemy spies.","pos":"noun","synonyms":["camouflage","mask","guise","pretense","garb"],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"","register":"countable, uncountable","wordFamily":["disguiseless","undisguise"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/disguise#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:156c100a797ae774cd","definition":"A change of behaviour resulting from intoxication, drunkenness.","example":"","pos":"noun","synonyms":["camouflage","mask","guise","pretense","garb"],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"archaic","regis